            "hunted-prey",
            "target:condition:concealed",
            {
              "not": "melee"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Twin Parry",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "Requirements Dmiri is wielding two melee weapons, one in each hand\n\n---\n\nDmiri uses her two weapons to parry attacks. Dmiri gains a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of her next turn, or a +2 circumstance bonus if either weapon has the parry trait. Dmiri loses this circumstance bonus if she no longer meet this ability's requirement.\n\nEffect: Twin Parry\n\nEffect: Twin Parry (Parry Trait)"
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Twin Takedown",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "Frequency once per round\n\nRequirement Dmiri is wielding two melee weapons, each in a different hand\n\n---\n\nDmiri swiftly attacks her hunted prey with both weapons. Make two Strikes against Dmiri 's hunted prey, one with each of the required weapons. If both hit the same hunted prey, combine their damage for the purpose of its resistances and weaknesses. Apply Dmiri 's multiple attack penalty to each Strike normally.",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "round"
      }
    }
